## How we run it

One spec: `tests/API/RAS/aiCoachDashboard.spec.js` · import `../../../path.js`. Each npm uses `--grep` (do not run the file with no grep).

| npm                                  | Tag                                        | When                 | Who                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |
| ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------ | -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `enableAiCoachSettings`              | `@aiCoachSettings`                         | Once per org         | Admin only                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |
| `createDataInAiCoachForDefaultUsers` | `@aiCoachDefaultUsers`                     | Once, rarely         | Names in `defaultUsers.json` that exist. Untouched GET-only. Ready profile+assessment. Full: 3 matched goals, then 2–3 chats + weekly session per chat                                                                           |
| `createDataInAiCoachDashboard`       | `@aiCoachDashboard`                        | Repeatable           | `USERCOUNT` other Learners (50, 100, 150…). Same N: A–E profile → assessment → goals/tasks (A/D 1 goal, B/C/E 2) → one chat. F GET data only. Profile/goals and chats in batches of 20. **No** scheduled sessions |
| `fullAiCoachCommand`                 | (run-s of settings + defaults + dashboard) | One Jenkins/npm pass | Default-user chats and pool chats are included                                                                                                                                                                                   |

Same file, three tests. Defaults never go in the `USERCOUNT` pool. Token collect, profile/goals, and pool chats all run in batches of 20. Import only `path.js`. `logger.info` / `logger.error`. No `console.log`. No UUIDs in testData. New AI Coach settings payload + apibuilder — do **not** edit `orgsettingPayload.js` / `orgSettingsApi.js` / `editOrgSettings.spec.js`. Reuse `urlData.orgSettingsUrl` + `orgSettingsHeaders`. Copy/skills live in `testData/aiCoach/`. Then package.json + Jenkins + CSV (same name) + `/sync-docs-with-framework`.

**Tokens:** Admin `generateToken` + `Authorization: Bearer` → API 2 only. Each learner: one `generateTokenLearner` + `percipio-id-token` + `locale: en-US` (`generateJwtTokenHeaders`) → all `/ai-coach/` calls. Do not log JWTs.

**Learner UI order (mandatory):** profile → self-assessment → goals. Before **any** `POST /goals` (API 10), GET API 6 `data` for that learner. Both `is_profile_completed` and `self_assessment_is_completed` must be `true`. If either is not true → log, skip goals **and chat** (do not POST 10). Same gate for default full users and `USERCOUNT` A–E. Profile PUT is skipped when already complete. **Assessment is always PUT** so Q2/Q4 (collaboration/trust and in-your-role) averages stay **above 4.5**. Re-runs still POST goals (they stack). Pool A–E: one chat only after goal+tasks succeed. Goal or task create failed → skip chat for that user. Default full: chats + API 15 only after **at least one** JSON goal was created. Missing skill after that match → skip that goal only, still chat if another goal landed.

**`USERCOUNT`:** only headcount we pass. Must be **50, 100, 150, 200…** (multiple of 50) or fail. Orgs have 1000+ learners; pick N. If eligible is below N → fail. Password from config unless the row has `passWord`. Pool: active, role Learner, `@noemail.com`, not a default login. Skip failed tokens and refill to N.

**Two jobs — do not mix them**

| Who                  | What we optimize for                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |
| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Default users**    | People we **log in as for demos**. Role and goal title must match the JSON row. Full logins post **all 3 JSON goals** (that is why Goals set > Users who set goals). Skill: exact planned name, a catalog name that contains it, another of the 20 names, or last an unused catalog skill so the title still lands. |
| **`USERCOUNT` pool** | Fills **admin Analytics → AI Coach** only. Rotate job roles. Mix the 20 skill names (and other catalog skills if a role cannot post a planned name). Short goals (`Improve <skill>`). These people are not for walkthroughs.                                                                                        |

Default **self-assessment** (ready + full): Q2/Q4 score **5**; other questions any valid answers — no per-login table. The **`USERCOUNT` mix** is what fills the Assessments charts (those two rating averages stay above 4.5). Random-user goals/roles fill the admin skill table. Default profiles, goals, tasks, and later chats stay matched to that login.

