## Assessment mix (M people) — dashboard bars

This mix is why the Assessments tab looks rich. **Every** Q1/Q3/Q5 choice (including Other) and **every** Q2/Q4 score 1–5 must get some people. Q2 and Q4 use **different** weight orders so the two rating charts do not match. 4 and 5 are much heavier so both averages stay above 4.5. Q1 vs Q3 vs Q5 shuffle the 9 weights so the three checkbox charts do not match.

Copy `question_id` from GET. `round_to_sum` so buckets add to M (or M×3).

Q2 is “How effective do you feel you are with building collaboration and trust with others?” Q4 is “How effective do you feel you are in your role?” Same mix as before (all 1–5), just more people on 4 and 5. Default ready/full score **5** on both. Assessment is re-PUT on re-runs so an org that already has low scores can recover.

**Q2 / Q4 people per score** = `round_to_sum(M * weight / 70)`:

| Score | Q2 weight | Q4 weight |
| ----- | --------- | --------- |
| 1     | 1         | 1         |
| 2     | 1         | 2         |
| 3     | 2         | 1         |
| 4     | 16        | 18        |
| 5     | 50        | 48        |

**Q1 / Q3 / Q5:** M×3 votes. `round_to_sum(M×3 * weight / 210)` with weights **8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 28, 32, 34, 36**. Other = the 8 slot. If Other is selected, `other_notes` is the JSON sentence for that question (not a placeholder). If Other is not selected, `other_notes` is null. **Shuffle that weight order per question.**

Q1: Creating innovative ideas or solutions; Meeting deadlines consistently; Managing or inspiring others; Communicating with clarity and intent; Demonstrates subject matter expertise; Solving complex problems proactively; Building cross-functional relationships; Successfully managing change or disruption; Other.

Q3: Following through on commitments; Setting clear expectations for others; Listening actively to understand; Removing blockers for the team; Staying flexible when plans change; Remaining solution-focused; Resolving conflict during challenges; Aligning work toward shared goals; Other.

Q5 (not the 20 goal names): Prioritizing the right work; Strategic thinking; Quality of work and attention to detail; Innovation and creative solutions; Proactive problem-solving; Making data-informed decisions; Functional or technical expertise; Coaching or mentoring others; Other.

Q6: unique short note per person.

